    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25811" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lanterna</span></b>  (ante-class. and later <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lā-terna</span></b> ), ae, f.
		Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαμπτήρ</span>, root in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάμπω</span>; cf. Lat. limpidus, lepor,
			lepidus, lĕpus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a lantern, lamp, torch</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">a portu illic nunc cum laterna huc advenit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Am. prol. 149</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laterna Punica,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Aul. 3, 6, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">linea lanterna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 4, 3, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hic caulis olebit lanternam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv. 5,
					88</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 11, 16, 16, §
		49</span></i>.</div>
